## Lore

Kwarla males who are not Mystics are Demon Hunters, the warriors and
hunters of a tribe. They are the reason travellers in the forests of the
east and north tell stories of fur-covered little people who came howling
out of the trees and tore a monster apart with their bare claws, then
carried off their wounded and melted back into the canopy without a word.

A Demon Hunter sees supernatural evil in black and white: there is no
bargaining with demons or foul creatures of magic, and the world has to be
cleared of such parasites if it is to regrow. He fights as part of a group
by preference, favors spears, clubs and axes of bone, tooth and Millennium
Tree timber, and is as likely to march up and call a demon lord out as to
lay an ambush for him.

## GM Notes

Pair this class with the Kwarla race, which carries the body: attributes,
M.D.C., claws, Claws of Vengeance, minor psionics and the racial bonuses.

Rogue Kwarla (G.M.''s option): a civilized Kwarla who has taken up houses,
guns and vehicles in the Outbacker way. Choose the Rogue variant: the skill
bonuses are halved and the character adds one piloting skill (typically
Horsemanship), three Technical skills without bonuses and one modern W.P.
Most are Anarchist, and other Kwarla regard them with disdain or worse,
though few lose the calling to fight supernatural evil.

The book prints no starting equipment and no money for the class. Tribal
Kwarla use spears, clubs, axes, boomerangs and, in the north, bows.
